# Docs-only direct-to-main exception

`AGENTS.md` is canonical. Docs-only narrative changes may go direct to `main`
only when the working tree is clean, local `main` exactly mirrors `origin/main`,
and the change touches no executable, config, schema, release, catalog,
rate-card, workflow, or runtime-affecting path.

## Docs-only means

- Markdown specs planning/audit prompts, runbooks, beta exploration reports,
  close-criteria or close-record notes, and narrative-only decision-log entries.
- Other non-executable documentation artifacts.

## Not docs-only

Use a feature branch and PR for:

- Any executable code: Swift, Go, CI/prod scripts, or shell shipped to providers.
- Money-path or auth paths:
  `phase4-coordinator/internal/{billing,buyer,auth,requestlog}/` and
  `phase5-gateway/internal/{router,auth}/`.
- Catalog, rate-card, `coordinator.yaml`, static JSON, CI workflows, schemas,
  release tooling, or anything that affects runtime behavior.

## Ship Sequence

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout main
git reset --hard origin/main   # only when main is clean of unique work
# edit docs...
git add <docs paths>
git commit -m "..."
git push origin main
```

When in doubt, use a branch and PR.
